Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790308799999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The strongest counterargument is that the trend keeps producing spiking highs that are not held: bar 86 reached 2771 with a 255.70-point upper tail and was followed by 27 sideways bars, and bar 117 now shows the same shape with high 2850 and close 2775.61 (74.39-point tail), so the current 'breakout' may be another overshoot rather than a durable spike.", "Trading-range behaviour dominates the window: bars 11-35, 50-83 and 87-113 are three multi-week ranges covering roughly 86 of 120 bars, so this market has repeatedly reverted to range after every strong leg, which weakens a trend-continuation label.", "The pullback is large relative to the leg: 216.69 points (~7.6%) from 2850 to 2633.31 in only three bars, and bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts the low 2641.70 of the breakout bar 117, a sign that the spike's momentum is already being absorbed.", "The last 20 bars are only net +207 (bar 101 close 2479.28 to bar 120 close 2686.59) while containing both a new high 2850 and a deep dip to 2358.62 (bar 111), i.e., two-sided rather than one-directional pressure."], "evidence_for": ["Acceptance above a multi-week range: four consecutive closes (2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90, 2775.61) above the 2557.46 top of the 27-bar bars 87-113 range, with a new window high at 2850 (bar 117).", "Swing progression is upward across the window: higher lows 1368.42 -> 1512.91 -> 1803.74 -> 2357.18 paired with higher highs 1944.39 -> 1974.46 -> 2771 -> 2850.", "The pullback after the breakout is being bought above the breakout level: bars 118-120 hold low 2633.31, and bar 120 closes 2686.59, 129 points above 2557.46 and in the upper 81% of its own 66.08 range.", "The 27-bar range (bars 87-113) resolved upward with follow-through bars 115 and 116 (closes 2632.98 and 2642.90) rather than immediately reversing, unlike the failed bar 61 (1974.46) and bar 107 (2680) probes inside earlier ranges."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window covers 120 closed D1 bars from open 1779926400000 to the final close 1790294399999; window low is 1368.42 (bar 10, close 1780790399999) and window high is 2850 (bar 117, close 1789948800000), a 108% advance from low to high.", "Bars 6-10 are five consecutive lower closes (1859.02, 1813.04, 1731.00, 1581.32, 1568.55), breaking the bars 1-5 range of 1958.77-2042.37; bar 6 opens 2006.06 with high 2006.17 and closes 1859.02.", "Bar 10 prints the window low 1368.42 but closes 1568.55, a 200.13-point lower tail (87% of its 230.85 range) - a climactic reversal bar rather than a clean bear trend bar.", "Bars 11-35 are two-sided and overlapping between high 1845.09 (bar 19) and low 1512.91 (bar 30); bar 30's 1512.91 is a higher low versus 1368.42.", "Bars 36-49 rally from 1597.72 (bar 36 low) to 1944.39 (bar 49 high) with consecutive bull closes 1889.93 and 1917.02 (bars 48-49).", "Bars 50-83 form a 34-bar overlapping range between 1803.74 (bar 51 low) and 1974.46 (bar 61 high); bar 61 opens 1953.92, tags 1974.46 and closes 1891.41, and bars 73 and 80 have ranges of only 13.24 and 10.41 (doji cluster).", "Bars 84-86 are a bull spike: bar 84 opens 1916.51 with low 1905.63 and closes 2252.16; bar 86 prints high 2771 but closes 2515.30, leaving a 255.70-point upper tail.", "Bars 87-113 hold a 27-bar range between 2357.18 (bar 98 low) and 2557.46 (bar 92 high); bar 107 spikes to 2680 and closes 2514.72 back inside the range.", "Bars 114-117 close 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61, all above the 2557.46 range high, and bar 117 reaches the new window high 2850.", "Bars 118-120 pull back from bar 118 high 2776.18 to bar 120 low 2633.31; bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts bar 117's low 2641.70, and bar 120 closes 2686.59 (81% of its 66.08 range) still 129 points above the 2557.46 breakout level."], "phase": "breakout-spike", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bear breakout of the bars 1-5 range 1958.77-2042.37, with five consecutive bear closes down to the 1368.42 low; bar 6 opens 2006.06 and closes 1859.02, bar 10 closes 1568.55.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780358400000, "upper_boundary": "2042.37"}, {"description": "Sell-climax reversal bar at the 1368.42 low: close 1568.55 with a 200.13-point lower tail, ending the bear spike and starting the basing process.", "end_time_ms": 1780790399999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780704000000, "upper_boundary": "1599.27"}, {"description": "Post-spike two-sided range with heavy overlap and alternating closes; high 1845.09 (bar 19), higher low 1512.91 (bar 30), roughly 1500-1850 area.", "end_time_ms": 1783036799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1845.09"}, {"description": "Bull leg from the 1597.72 low (bar 36) to the 1944.39 high (bar 49), continued by a pullback low of 1803.74 (bar 51).", "end_time_ms": 1784073599999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "1597.72", "start_time_ms": 1782950400000, "upper_boundary": "1944.39"}, {"description": "34-bar overlapping range between 1803.74 (bar 51 low) and 1974.46 (bar 61 high); the bar 61 probe above 1974.46 failed and closed 1891.41, and bars 73 and 80 are very small doji bars.", "end_time_ms": 1787097600000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1803.74", "start_time_ms": 1784160000000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the 1800-1975 range: bar 84 rises from 1916.51 to close 2252.16, and bar 86 spikes to 2771 before closing 2515.30 (buy climax with a 255.70-point upper tail).", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "27-bar range after the spike between 2357.18 (bar 98 low) and 2557.46 (bar 92 high); bar 107 overshoots to 2680 but closes 2514.72 back inside the range.", "end_time_ms": 1789689599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2557.46"}, {"description": "Four-bar breakout above the 2557.46 range top: closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.90 and 2775.61, with bar 117 printing the window high 2850 (74.39-point upper tail).", "end_time_ms": 1789948800000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Three-bar pullback from bar 118 high 2776.18 to bar 120 low 2633.31 that holds above the 2557.46 breakout level; bar 119's low 2641.37 undercuts bar 117's low 2641.70 and bar 120 closes 2686.59 near the top of its range.", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2776.18"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Two or more consecutive closes above 2776.18 (bar 118 high) would confirm the bars 114-117 leg as a continuing spike and keep the read as bull breakout.", "A daily close back below 2557.46 (the bars 87-113 range top) would mark the breakout as failed and revert the primary read to trading-range with an upper boundary near 2850.", "A close below bar 120's low 2633.31 followed by a lower high below 2776.18 would shift the always-in to short and raise the higher-high MTR-like interpretation of 2771 versus 2850.", "Continued overlapping closes between roughly 2633 and 2776 with small bodies would move the phase from breakout-spike toward channel or range without changing the bullish regime label."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790294399999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The window's dominant displacement is upward (open 2454.35 -> close 2686.59) and the bull leg's major higher lows (2358.62 at 1789488000000; 2568.16 at 1789876800000) remain far below the latest low 2633.31, so the larger uptrend structure is not broken.", "The largest-range bars of the window are bull bars closing in the upper half or at highs (2457.12 -> 2555.52 with a 2680.00 high; 2507.15 -> 2578.60; 2642.90 -> 2664.73; 2658.81 -> 2723.15), which is the profile of a bull flag rather than a completed top.", "The 2633.31-2648.49 zone attracted buyers twice (bars 1790179200000 and 1790251200000), and bars 1790251200000-1790265600000 close 2682.25 and 2694.09 back at the top of the recent band, so the bear breakout has not produced a second leg down in the last eight bars.", "The mtr-like reading is unconfirmed: the bear breakout bar 1790164800000 was answered by a three-bar recovery, no bar closes below the last major higher low 2568.16, and the last close 2686.59 is above the pre-breakout range lows of bars 1790193600000-1790222400000."], "evidence_for": ["21 consecutive bars (1789992000000-1790294399999) trade inside 2633.31-2804.59 with heavy overlap: no close above 2772.99 after 1790020800000 and the final 8 bars hold a 66.08-point band versus 156.10 points for bars 1790006400000-1790179200000.", "Each push after the high fails at a lower level (2850.00 -> 2804.59 -> 2786.81 -> 2778.33 -> 2767.30 -> 2699.39), so the climax high has not been retested.", "Bar 1790164800000 is a bear bar closing 2659.00 below the 2716.01 shelf that bars 1790049600000-1790116800000 held, and the recovery high 2699.39 stays under it: the recent bull micro-structure of higher lows has failed (2633.31 under 2716.01).", "A 126.85-point upper tail climax bar at 2850.00 followed by 21 bars of two-sided, overlapping trade matches a post-climax trading range rather than immediate trend resumption; the last bar is an inside bar (2695.78/2676.02), i.e. a small range inside the larger range.", "Two-sided closes in the final stretch (2647.90, 2682.25, 2694.09, 2686.59) and mid-block position near 2718 leave neither side with acceptance, so the directional read stays balanced with low always-in relevance."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window opens 2454.35 and closes 2686.59; window low 2358.62 (bar opening 1789488000000) and window high 2850.00 (bar opening 1789977600000).", "Bars 1788566400000-1789128000000 (first 39 bars) rotate between 2411.04 and 2528.80; the next bar (open 2457.12) spikes to 2680.00 but closes 2555.52, leaving a 124.48 upper tail.", "Bars opening 1789761600000-1789977600000 stair-step up with bull bodies closing near highs (e.g. 2507.15 -> 2578.60; 2579.97 -> 2636.28; 2642.90 -> 2664.73); bar 1789977600000 opens 2658.81, prints 2850.00 and closes 2723.15 (126.85 upper tail).", "After that high the last 21 bars (1789992000000 to 1790280000000) overlap inside 2633.31-2804.59; no close above 2772.99 after 2775.61 (bar 1790020800000) and no close above 2772.99 again in the final 18 bars.", "Lower-high sequence after the peak: 2850.00 -> 2804.59 (bar 1790020800000) -> 2786.81 (1790136000000) -> 2778.33 (1790121600000) -> 2767.30 (1790107200000) -> 2699.39 (1790265600000).", "Bar 1790164800000 (open 2726.71) breaks to 2648.49 and closes 2659.00, below the 2716.01-2729.14 lows held by bars 1790049600000-1790107200000; the later rally high 2699.39 stays below that broken shelf, so the last swing low 2633.31 (1790236800000) is under the prior swing low 2716.01.", "The final 8 bars (1790179200000-1790294399999) contract to a 2633.31-2699.39 band with closes 2647.90-2694.09; the last bar (open 2694.09, high 2695.78, low 2676.02, close 2686.59) is an inside bar within the prior bar's 2660.49-2699.39 range."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Post-climax trading range at the top of the window: bars 1790006400000-1790294399999 overlap inside 2633.31-2804.59 (exact window extremes of that block), with lower highs 2804.59 -> 2786.81 -> 2767.30 -> 2699.39, repeated upper/lower tails and no close above 2772.99 after 1790020800000. Price sits near the middle of the block (midpoint about 2718).", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790006400000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Bull leg with rising pullback lows from the 2358.62 low (1789488000000) to the 2850.00 high (1789977600000): higher lows 2358.62 -> 2568.16 (1789876800000) -> 2716.01 (1790049600000), bull spike bars and closes in the upper half on most bars of the leg; the last low 2633.31 remains above the last major higher low 2568.16.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850.00"}, {"description": "Buy-climax spike bar: open 2658.81, high 2850.00, close 2723.15 (upper tail 126.85) inside a 2658.06-2850.00 range; the next bar prints 2795.00 but closes 2754.31, so no bar closes near 2850.00. This overshoot high is the range-top reference.", "end_time_ms": 1790006400000, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "2658.06", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850.00"}, {"description": "Possible major-trend-reversal shape of the bull leg: buy climax at 2850.00 (1789977600000), lower high 2804.59 (1790020800000), bear breakout bar 1790164800000 (open 2726.71, low 2648.49, close 2659.00) below the 2716.01-2729.14 shelf, then a rally that stalls at 2699.39 (1790265600000) below the broken shelf. Unconfirmed: no close below the last major higher low 2568.16 and the final three bars recover to 2694.09.", "end_time_ms": 1790294399999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850.00"}, {"description